Round array, cache misses between processes
===========================================

Part of CACHE_FRAMEWORK: kernels kept as a separate set for cache studies
(cache locking and cache-miss analysis).

What it tests
-------------

Cache interference between processes of one partition that share an array: each
process touches a different 4 KB "way" of the array line by line.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with five periodic processes.

Five processes (ROUND_ARRAY_A653_PROC_0..4), period 100 ms, each increment one
byte per 32-byte line of a 5 x 4 KB array. P1 has two 500 ms windows per 1000
ms major frame.

Expected output
---------------

A "." per process activation.

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/round_array_cache_miss/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/round_array_cache_miss/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
